    "question": {
      ":question/id": "69283293-9f74-5957-a884-9017a43d8a08",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + y + z &=6 \\\\ x + 2 y + z &=8 \\\\ x + y + 2 z &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=3$, $y=2$, and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle 3,2,1\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
